// SOURCE: examples/gpu/pathtrace/main.vl
// REQUIRES: metal
// LINK: std::gpu and std::window name the frameworks they link
// (0.25.4) The window's own event loop with no display, driven by a
// script (std::window, VOLE_WINDOW_SCRIPT): a click on the panel's
// "Mirror field" button (a press, a frame, a release: the panel is
// immediate-mode) changes the lab's scene. The panel then names it in the
// SCENE row and highlights its button; before the click both show Studio.
// ENV: VOLE_WINDOW_SCRIPT=size 640x400; frames 2; move 470 345; frames 1; press left 470 345; frames 1; release left 470 345; frames 2; shot pathtrace-script.ppm; frames 1
// EXPECT: pathtrace: native window + Metal GPU + immediate-mode UI
// EXPECT-PPM: pathtrace-script.ppm tests/golden/pathtrace-script.ppm region 440,90,170,22 tolerance 8 allow 1%
// EXPECT-PPM: pathtrace-script.ppm tests/golden/pathtrace-script-2.ppm region 334,326,160,44 tolerance 8 allow 1%
